1
00:00:41,012 --> 00:00:41,738
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Earth,</i></font>

2
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:43,575
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>before the war.</i></font>

3
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:46,743
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>New York,</i></font>

4
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:48,473
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>before I was born.</i></font>

5
00:00:49,995 --> 00:00:51,690
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>A place I have only seen pictures of.</i></font>

6
00:00:54,615 --> 00:00:55,807
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I know you...</i></font>

7
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,276
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>But we have never met.</i></font>

8
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,267
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I am with you...</i></font>

9
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,345
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>But I don't know your name.</i></font>

10
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,439
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I know I am dreaming.</i></font>

11
00:01:08,412 --> 00:01:09,992
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>But it feels like more than that.</i></font>

12
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:13,812
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>It feels like a memory.</i></font>

13
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,250
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>How can that be?</i></font>

14
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:31,377
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>March 14th, 2077.</i></font>

15
00:01:32,461 --> 00:01:35,018
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Five years since
the mandatory memory wipe.</i></font>

16
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,784
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>And I am still haunted by these dreams.</i></font>

17
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:43,500
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Victoria and I were assigned together.</i></font>

18
00:01:44,238 --> 00:01:46,803
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>In two weeks, our mission here will be
finished,</i></font>

19
00:01:46,828 --> 00:01:48,242
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>and we will I join the others.</i></font>

20
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,849
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>But the questions I ask,</i></font>

21
00:01:50,873 --> 00:01:51,953
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>she doesn't.</i></font>

22
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,727
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>The things I wonder about,</i></font>

23
00:01:54,142 --> 00:01:55,218
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>she won't.</i></font>

24
00:01:56,799 --> 00:01:59,929
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>It's been half a century since
the scavengers destroyed our moon.</i></font>

25
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,527
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Forced to leave their
own dying planet,</i></font>

26
00:02:02,933 --> 00:02:04,410
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>they came to take ours.</i></font>

27
00:02:05,549 --> 00:02:08,112
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Without the moon,
the Earth was thrown into chaos.</i></font>

28
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:10,718
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Earthquakes toppled cities within hours.</i></font>

29
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:13,742
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Tsunamis wiped out what remained.</i></font>

30
00:02:14,644 --> 00:02:15,999
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Then came the invasion.</i></font>

31
00:02:17,517 --> 00:02:18,953
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>We did what we had to do.</i></font>

32
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,301
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>We used the nukes.</i></font>

33
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:24,966
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>We won the war,</i></font>

34
00:02:25,606 --> 00:02:26,981
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>but lost the planet.</i></font>

35
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:28,928
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Left it contaminated.</i></font>

36
00:02:29,309 --> 00:02:30,845
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Most of it uninhabitable.</i></font>

37
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:35,386
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>What remained of humanity
had to leave the Earth.</i></font>

38
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,188
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>We built the Tet,</i></font>

39
00:02:38,815 --> 00:02:40,159
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>our mission control.</i></font>

40
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:43,844
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>A temporary space station
before the migration to Titan,</i></font>

41
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,047
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Saturn's largest moon.</i></font>

42
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:47,969
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Everyone is there now.</i></font>

43
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:49,699
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Well,</i></font>

44
00:02:50,094 --> 00:02:51,149
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>almost everyone.</i></font>

45
00:02:52,726 --> 00:02:54,287
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Until our tour is complete,</i></font>

46
00:02:54,669 --> 00:02:56,162
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Vika and I do our job.</i></font>

47
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,535
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>We protect the hydro rigs,</i></font>

48
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:02,005
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>which convert Earth's sea water
into fusion energy for the new colony.</i></font>

49
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,915
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>The survival of humanity depends on it.</i></font>

50
00:03:10,371 --> 00:03:11,446
Thank you for the coffee.

51
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:15,365
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Remnants of the scavenger army
continue to disrupt the operation.</i></font>

52
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:17,998
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>They attack our drones at night,</i></font>

53
00:03:18,467 --> 00:03:20,349
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>and try to kill me during the day.</i></font>

54
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,820
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>There is still fight in them,
but I don't know why.</i></font>

55
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,390
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Mission says we have done well.</i></font>

56
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,447
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>That we are...</i></font>

57
00:03:29,619 --> 00:03:30,850
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>an effective team.</i></font>

58
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,818
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Vika is my communications officer.</i></font>

59
00:03:44,328 --> 00:03:45,716
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>She keeps an eye on me.</i></font>

60
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,826
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I handle drone maintenance.</i></font>

61
00:03:49,748 --> 00:03:51,286
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>The drones watch everything.</i></font>

62
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,690
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Vika can't wait to go.</i></font>

63
00:03:54,938 --> 00:03:56,682
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Me, I am not so sure.</i></font>

64
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,901
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I can't shake the feeling that Earth,</i></font>

65
00:04:01,373 --> 00:04:03,055
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>in spite of all that's happened...</i></font>

66
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:05,461
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Earth is still my home.</i></font>

67
00:04:31,737 --> 00:04:33,213
Jack Harper, Tech-49.

68
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,652
Morning Bob.

69
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,665
<i>Tower, comm check.</i>

70
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,968
<i>Drone Maintenance Technician 49,</i>

71
00:05:13,992 --> 00:05:15,109
<i>hydro rig support.</i>

72
00:05:15,134 --> 00:05:16,874
All Bubbleship systems are green.

73
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,127
I am good to go.

74
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:21,567
Copy, Tech-49, you are cleared.
Be careful out there.

75
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,727
Always am.

76
00:05:22,751 --> 00:05:23,649
No, you are not.

77
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,063
Yeah, you are right.

78
00:05:25,696 --> 00:05:26,884
I got to work on that.

79
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:38,402
Alright, Tet's coming online in 30 seconds.

80
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:40,310
Relaying hydro rig coordinates now.

81
00:05:40,354 --> 00:05:41,387
<i>Confirm visual.</i>

82
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,252
I got them.

83
00:05:47,494 --> 00:05:49,385
Hydro rigs are sucking seawater.

84
00:05:51,223 --> 00:05:52,270
You got them, Bob?

85
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,696
Drone 185 looks good.

86
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,553
Jack, we have got two drones down.

87
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,115
Shit.

88
00:06:08,290 --> 00:06:09,894
Stand by, Mission coming online.

89
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,282
<i>And we have Tet contact.</i>

90
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:17,678
Morning, boss.

91
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,522
<i>Tower 49, this is Mission Control.</i>

92
00:06:21,552 --> 00:06:23,634
<i>How you all doing this lovely morning?</i>

93
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,456
Another day in paradise Sally.

94
00:06:25,691 --> 00:06:27,175
Uploading data now.

95
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:30,468
49 mission log. Day 1642.

96
00:06:30,492 --> 00:06:31,722
Hydro rig support.

97
00:06:31,763 --> 00:06:33,847
I have two...
<i>You have two drones offline.</i>

98
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,251
<i>Perimeter is compromised.</i>

99
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,735
Copy that, relaying to Tech.
Stand by.

100
00:06:39,665 --> 00:06:40,305
Jack?

101
00:06:40,829 --> 00:06:43,334
166 is down in Grid 37.

102
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,566
Linking to beacon now.

103
00:06:45,933 --> 00:06:47,145
<i>You will go there first.</i>

104
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:48,855
Got it.

105
00:06:49,066 --> 00:06:49,973
On my way.

106
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:55,321
<i>Mission, Tech-49 is en route to Grid 37 now.</i>

107
00:06:55,574 --> 00:06:57,655
<i>Can you plug that hole with Drone 109?</i>

108
00:06:57,726 --> 00:06:59,490
Negative, 109 is in the dock.

109
00:06:59,915 --> 00:07:00,986
Still waiting for parts.

110
00:07:01,518 --> 00:07:03,680
<i>Jack better find those drones
and get them flying.</i>

111
00:07:03,705 --> 00:07:05,782
<i>Those rigs can't be exposed overnight.</i>

112
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:07,929
Copy that.

113
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:33,090
<i>Tower, didn't he fix 166 recently?</i>

114
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,049
Jack has fixed all the drones recently.

115
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:37,314
And, if we had the parts
that we have been asking for,

116
00:07:37,339 --> 00:07:38,882
we would not be running
a skeleton crew down here.

117
00:07:38,907 --> 00:07:41,202
<i>Understood.
We are doing the best we can.</i>

118
00:07:41,418 --> 00:07:42,866
<i>Are you an effective team?</i>

119
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,382
We are an effective team.

120
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:52,372
<i>Your directive today is to rehabilitate 166</i>

121
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:54,204
<i>and find 172.</i>

122
00:07:54,293 --> 00:07:55,670
<i>Get them flying by sundown,</i>

123
00:07:55,695 --> 00:07:58,585
<i>and I will buy you two a round of
drinks when you get up to the Tet.</i>

124
00:07:58,610 --> 00:07:59,828
You had better be ready Sally.

125
00:07:59,853 --> 00:08:00,760
Two weeks now,

126
00:08:00,892 --> 00:08:01,986
we are keeping track.

127
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,462
Ok.

128
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,807
Come on Bob.
Work with me here buddy.

129
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,497
Tech-49?

130
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:20,130
<i>Tech-49?</i>

131
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:24,658
<i>Jack?</i>

132
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,448
Copy Tower.

133
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,127
What happened?
I lost you for a second.

134
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:29,807
Really?

135
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:32,820
<i>Coming up on location.</i>

136
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:46,919
There it is.

137
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,458
I have got multiple scav kills.

138
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:52,082
Drone 166 put up a hell of a fight.

139
00:08:53,169 --> 00:08:54,250
Got any movement?

140
00:08:54,749 --> 00:08:56,861
No sign of scavenger activity but...

141
00:08:57,089 --> 00:08:58,818
I have got limited visibility here Jack,

142
00:08:58,842 --> 00:09:00,332
due to low angle of Mission.

143
00:09:00,397 --> 00:09:01,314
<i>Copy that.</i>

144
00:09:01,613 --> 00:09:02,594
I am coming in hot.

145
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,309
Starting repairs.

146
00:09:31,925 --> 00:09:32,878
Watch my back.

147
00:09:35,093 --> 00:09:36,133
I always do.

148
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,521
You know, I read about this game.

149
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,443
It was played right here.

150
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,293
<i>The last Super Bowl.</i>

151
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,160
Please don't tell me it was a classic.

152
00:10:10,378 --> 00:10:11,551
A classic game.

153
00:10:14,073 --> 00:10:15,191
Down by four.

154
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:18,564
<i>The ball</i>

155
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:21,165
<i>was on the 50-yard line.</i>

156
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:23,321
<i>Seconds left on the clock.</i>

157
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,370
The ball is snapped,

158
00:10:27,706 --> 00:10:29,117
and the QB fumbles.

159
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,334
Disaster.

160
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,643
Looks like the game is over.

161
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,440
I am reading the whole
central core off-alignment.

162
00:10:39,464 --> 00:10:41,162
You don't have the necessary
tools down there.

163
00:10:41,379 --> 00:10:43,277
<i>And a new fuel cell is
not going to fix that.</i>

164
00:10:46,614 --> 00:10:48,219
But this QB runs back,
<i>Jack?</i>

165
00:10:48,243 --> 00:10:49,480
<i>And picks up his own fumble.</i>

166
00:10:49,505 --> 00:10:50,705
Hold on, what did you just do?

167
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:53,316
<i>There is a wall of linebackers
closing in on him.</i>

168
00:10:55,421 --> 00:10:56,978
<i>So he throws a long ball,</i>

169
00:10:57,002 --> 00:10:59,616
<i>with no idea who is at the other end.</i>

170
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:01,468
A Hail Mary.

171
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,601
Eighty-thousand people on their feet,

172
00:11:05,626 --> 00:11:07,776
watching this ball sail through the air.

173
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:10,616
Downfield,

174
00:11:11,304 --> 00:11:12,368
is a rookie...

175
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,936
wide receiver, third string.

176
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,631
He just leaps out of the pack.

177
00:11:19,618 --> 00:11:21,108
Touchdown!

178
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:41,879
Contact! West contact!

179
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:45,542
<i>Jack?</i>

180
00:11:47,221 --> 00:11:48,347
It's ok Vika.

181
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,354
It's just a dog.

182
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,122
Hey.

183
00:11:59,984 --> 00:12:00,833
Now go on.

184
00:12:01,067 --> 00:12:02,037
You got to get out of here.

185
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,118
Go on, get!

186
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:06,094
Get out of here! Go!

187
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:16,492
<i>Tech-49, Jack Harper.</i>

188
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:44,877
You are welcome.

189
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:49,590
166...

190
00:12:49,987 --> 00:12:51,042
is back online.

191
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:01,039
Two drones shot down today.

192
00:13:01,263 --> 00:13:03,735
Ten fuel cells stolen in just over a month.

193
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:05,468
These scavs are getting bolder.

194
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,156
<i>Well, the hydro rigs
are taking all the water.</i>

195
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:11,551
Once we are gone, they will have
nothing but dust and radiation.

196
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,467
<i>This is bullshit.</i>

197
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,319
We won the war.

198
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,311
Now we have to leave.

199
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,300
Two more weeks Jack.

200
00:13:23,215 --> 00:13:24,949
<i>Then we will be on our way to Titan.</i>

201
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,605
Yep.

202
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,667
That drone is out there somewhere.

203
00:13:33,258 --> 00:13:34,719
We just have to find it.

204
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:38,243
Without a beacon, that's like
finding a needle in a haystack.

205
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,665
So we go to our ground game.

206
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:31,585
Tower,

207
00:15:32,186 --> 00:15:33,947
located 172,

208
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,791
down a sinkhole.

209
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,299
No visual but I can hear it.

210
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,215
Tet's so far off angle, I can barely see you.

211
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:43,350
How is it look?

212
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,100
It's good, it's good.

213
00:15:46,124 --> 00:15:47,975
There is no sign of scav activity on top.

214
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:50,257
<i>Tet is offline in 15 minutes.</i>

215
00:15:51,843 --> 00:15:53,310
<i>After that, you are on your own.</i>

216
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,710
<i>Mission this is Tower 49.</i>

217
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:16,255
<i>Jack has located drone 172.</i>

218
00:16:16,562 --> 00:16:18,062
<i>Engaged in recovery now.</i>

219
00:16:18,613 --> 00:16:19,675
Requesting backup,

220
00:16:19,699 --> 00:16:21,650
to his location ASAP.

221
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,699
I have got a visual on Drone 172.

222
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:54,580
Jack?

223
00:18:01,172 --> 00:18:03,055
What the hell?

224
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:08,078
Shit.

225
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:49,112
Jack!

226
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,667
Tech-49, Jack Harper.

227
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,589
Jack Harper, Tech-49!

228
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:29,831
Hey!

229
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:17,391
Oh, no.

230
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,477
Come on.

231
00:21:21,502 --> 00:21:23,399
Not my goddamn bike!

232
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:32,229
How can a man die better
Than facing fearful odds

233
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:35,417
For the ashes of his fathers
And the temples of his Gods

234
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:36,393
Jack?

235
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:38,762
Yep,

236
00:22:38,973 --> 00:22:40,113
I will be right there.

237
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:59,232
How does 109 look?

238
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:00,959
Can it fly?

239
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:01,788
Barely.

240
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:05,413
And without armor, she is a sitting duck.

241
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:08,292
Well, I will talk to Sally,

242
00:23:08,316 --> 00:23:10,003
about that shielding in the morning.

243
00:23:10,177 --> 00:23:11,014
Again.

244
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:17,551
What,

245
00:23:17,723 --> 00:23:19,184
Jack Harper?

246
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:28,950
Where did you get this?

247
00:23:29,777 --> 00:23:31,142
It was growing in...

248
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:48,960
Come on Jack, you know the regulations.
I know you think I am a stickler

249
00:23:48,985 --> 00:23:51,636
but you have no idea what kind of toxins
could be in something like that.

250
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:55,214
It's a flower, Vika.
Yeah, that's not the point.

251
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:57,927
It's that we are so close to the end,

252
00:23:57,952 --> 00:24:00,107
and the last thing that we need
is you putting it all at risk.

253
00:24:02,425 --> 00:24:03,185
Ok.

254
00:24:07,640 --> 00:24:09,768
Every day, you have to go down there,

255
00:24:10,800 --> 00:24:12,457
and see what was lost.

256
00:24:14,583 --> 00:24:16,168
But we have done our job Jack.

257
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:21,947
It's time to go.

258
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:30,415
I don't think they were trying to...

259
00:24:30,439 --> 00:24:31,585
kill me today.

260
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:33,445
The scavs.

261
00:24:39,262 --> 00:24:40,536
They were trying to catch me.

262
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:47,151
Well, they can't have you.

263
00:25:04,602 --> 00:25:05,596
Come on.

264
00:26:03,040 --> 00:26:04,551
You should come with me sometime,

265
00:26:04,879 --> 00:26:05,956
before we leave.

266
00:26:07,586 --> 00:26:08,972
There is a place I found,

267
00:26:09,183 --> 00:26:10,464
I would like to show you.

268
00:26:14,979 --> 00:26:16,618
I will show you something.

269
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:20,204
Hey, hey!

270
00:27:42,539 --> 00:27:43,463
Oh, my God.

271
00:27:52,866 --> 00:27:56,304
<i>It was a six-stage meltdown
from inside the hydro rig's core.</i>

272
00:27:57,040 --> 00:27:58,530
<i>It's offline permanently.</i>

273
00:27:58,617 --> 00:28:01,575
<i>Tower 49, you have put
the whole operation at risk.</i>

274
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:03,682
<i>I need to know exactly what happened.</i>

275
00:28:03,707 --> 00:28:06,632
<i>Jack believes the scavs
weaponized one of the stolen fuel cells</i>

276
00:28:06,657 --> 00:28:08,305
<i>and got it into the suction.</i>

277
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:09,895
<i>Tower hold.</i>

278
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:12,429
Tower?

279
00:28:12,895 --> 00:28:15,669
I have got a rogue signal in Grid 37.
Are you seeing this?

280
00:28:16,240 --> 00:28:16,997
Yes.

281
00:28:17,601 --> 00:28:18,785
<i>It's got to be scav.</i>

282
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:21,041
It's not one of ours.

283
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:22,439
Jack,

284
00:28:23,095 --> 00:28:25,361
the signal is being directed off-planet.

285
00:28:26,220 --> 00:28:27,268
On my way.

286
00:28:28,579 --> 00:28:33,215
<i>Tower, our logs show you are missing
an additional nine fuel cells.</i>

287
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:35,695
<i>Can you confirm?</i>
Negative, Mission that number is 10.

288
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:38,921
Drone 172 was lost last night.

289
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:42,271
109 is combat ready as soon
as we get that shielding.

290
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:45,539
We can cover the remaining rigs
with drones in the field.

291
00:28:45,540 --> 00:28:46,466
I have run the numbers.

292
00:28:46,491 --> 00:28:48,334
<i>We will do the numbers up here Tower.</i>

293
00:28:48,412 --> 00:28:50,858
<i>I am tasking the drones to defensive positions.</i>

294
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:52,370
Copy.

295
00:28:52,395 --> 00:28:56,175
<i>Our job is to run those rigs.
Your directive is to protect them.</i>

296
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:58,226
<i>We cannot afford to lose another.</i>

297
00:28:58,251 --> 00:28:59,540
<i>Do you copy?</i>

298
00:29:00,040 --> 00:29:00,878
Copy.

299
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,141
<i>Are you and Jack an effective team?</i>

300
00:29:03,440 --> 00:29:04,445
Damn right we are.

301
00:29:14,674 --> 00:29:15,513
Jack?

302
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:18,482
You are right on top of it.
Do you have a visual?

303
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:21,755
<i>Jack?</i>

304
00:29:22,560 --> 00:29:23,208
Yeah,

305
00:29:23,301 --> 00:29:24,200
I got it.

306
00:31:09,646 --> 00:31:11,448
They have some kind of a repeater.

307
00:31:12,970 --> 00:31:14,027
The scavs...

308
00:31:14,293 --> 00:31:16,730
are using the building,
as an antenna.

309
00:31:17,625 --> 00:31:18,626
Can you decrypt?

310
00:31:23,280 --> 00:31:24,875
It's a set of coordinates.

311
00:31:25,524 --> 00:31:26,928
<i>Grid 17.</i>

312
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:29,187
<i>It's a goddamn homing beacon.</i>

313
00:31:29,356 --> 00:31:30,562
Grid 17.

314
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:32,361
What the hell is out there?

315
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:37,707
Nothing.
It's the middle of nowhere.

316
00:31:39,137 --> 00:31:40,420
<i>What is going on?</i>

317
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:43,896
Why would the scavs send
a signal off-planet Jack?

318
00:31:47,120 --> 00:31:48,345
I am shutting it down.

319
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:04,282
Tech-49, check your course.
You are headed right for the border.

320
00:32:05,572 --> 00:32:08,407
<i>That radiation will cook you from
the inside before you know it.</i>

321
00:32:09,320 --> 00:32:10,810
It's ok Vika.
I see it.

322
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:14,587
I am gonna do a...

323
00:32:14,954 --> 00:32:15,964
perimeter check,

324
00:32:16,144 --> 00:32:17,568
before I head home.

325
00:32:19,010 --> 00:32:20,190
I may go off-comm.

326
00:32:21,399 --> 00:32:23,565
Jack, we should keep in contact.
Just let me know where you are.

327
00:32:25,190 --> 00:32:26,190
<i>Do you copy?</i>

328
00:32:28,360 --> 00:32:29,538
<i>Jack do you copy?</i>

329
00:32:37,804 --> 00:32:38,806
That's right Bob.

330
00:32:40,713 --> 00:32:42,028
You know where we are going.

331
00:34:24,120 --> 00:34:25,203
Are you gonna miss me?

332
00:34:34,760 --> 00:34:36,076
I am gonna miss this place.

333
00:34:38,120 --> 00:34:39,373
It would have been great.

334
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:48,995
It would have been great.

335
00:35:54,720 --> 00:35:56,688
<i>Vika? Vika, did you get that?</i>

336
00:35:56,778 --> 00:35:58,095
<i>Jack, where have you been?</i>

337
00:35:58,520 --> 00:36:00,358
An object came down in 17.

338
00:36:00,640 --> 00:36:01,976
That's the beacon coordinates.

339
00:36:02,109 --> 00:36:02,913
Exactly.

340
00:36:03,041 --> 00:36:04,951
<i>I saw it.
Some sort of vessel.</i>

341
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:06,632
Jack, Mission is almost offline.

342
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:07,983
<i>I am en route now.</i>

343
00:36:09,320 --> 00:36:11,862
Mission, we have an unidentified
object impact in 17.

344
00:36:11,887 --> 00:36:14,221
It came down at coordinates
sent by a scav beacon.

345
00:36:14,246 --> 00:36:15,375
My tech is en route now.

346
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:17,309
<i>Tower, we are going offline soon but...</i>

347
00:36:17,334 --> 00:36:19,809
<i>but drones are already
mobile and executing.</i>

348
00:36:19,834 --> 00:36:21,563
<i>Have your tech stand down.</i>

349
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:22,658
Copy.

350
00:36:23,720 --> 00:36:25,869
Jack, Mission wants you to stand down.
The drones will handle it.

351
00:36:26,022 --> 00:36:27,368
<i>That's a negative Tower.</i>

352
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:29,815
With Tet offline, we need our eyes on this.

353
00:36:30,240 --> 00:36:32,083
I want to know this site is secure.

354
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:37,559
Sally, my tech is concerned about
the security of the site.

355
00:36:37,560 --> 00:36:40,015
<i>Tower, you have lost
enough assets for today.</i>

356
00:36:40,040 --> 00:36:42,062
<i>Keep your tech out of there.
Do you copy?</i>

357
00:36:42,087 --> 00:36:43,327
Copy, Command I am...

358
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:50,655
Jack, Command wants you to stand down.

359
00:36:50,679 --> 00:36:51,923
The drones will handle this.

360
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:53,236
<i>I am on site.</i>

361
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:54,939
<i>Jack.</i>

362
00:36:55,122 --> 00:36:57,353
<i>I don't have eyes on you.
Command is offline.</i>

363
00:36:58,080 --> 00:36:58,746
Vika,

364
00:36:59,098 --> 00:37:00,431
I think it's one of ours.

365
00:37:03,520 --> 00:37:05,108
This thing is ancient.
It looks...

366
00:37:06,040 --> 00:37:07,022
pre-war.

367
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:09,577
The scavs brought this thing down, Jack.

368
00:37:09,920 --> 00:37:11,251
There is no sign of scavs.

369
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:12,895
<i>Technician, this is your Control.</i>

370
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:14,262
I am ordering you to pull out,

371
00:37:14,286 --> 00:37:16,083
and return to the tower immediately.

372
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:18,634
Touching down.

373
00:37:57,069 --> 00:37:58,218
They are human.

374
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:06,314
Tower,

375
00:38:06,782 --> 00:38:08,255
we have got survivors.

376
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:10,931
There are four.

377
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:13,125
Check it, five survivors.

378
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:15,791
They are human.

379
00:38:48,673 --> 00:38:49,644
Stand down!

380
00:38:50,120 --> 00:38:52,088
Vika, the drones are firing on survivors.

381
00:38:52,113 --> 00:38:53,914
Jack, the Tet is offline, I-I...

382
00:38:54,331 --> 00:38:55,695
I don't have control.

383
00:38:55,920 --> 00:38:57,005
Stand down!

384
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:06,184
<i>Jack Harper, Tech-49.</i>

385
00:39:14,682 --> 00:39:16,643
<i>Back off, you son of a bitch!</i>

386
00:39:24,240 --> 00:39:25,844
<i>Back off!</i>

387
00:40:32,360 --> 00:40:33,407
Open the door.

388
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:37,532
Vika!

389
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:53,105
Get the med kit.

390
00:40:54,360 --> 00:40:55,480
Get the med kit!

391
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:11,116
This has to be reported.

392
00:41:11,141 --> 00:41:14,145
Be sure and report that the drones
killed the crew from one of our own ships.

393
00:41:14,640 --> 00:41:16,051
See what Command makes of that.

394
00:41:23,880 --> 00:41:25,933
It's breathing fluid.
Just let her get it out.

395
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:38,348
Jack.

396
00:42:05,080 --> 00:42:06,803
Here. You are still dehydrated.

397
00:42:22,490 --> 00:42:23,572
Where are we?

398
00:42:24,913 --> 00:42:26,031
I am Victoria,

399
00:42:26,719 --> 00:42:28,023
this is Jack.

400
00:42:31,880 --> 00:42:32,862
What's your name?

401
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:37,492
I am Julia.

402
00:42:38,320 --> 00:42:39,606
Julia...

403
00:42:39,873 --> 00:42:41,609
I am sorry for what I have to tell you,

404
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:44,589
but you were in a crash.

405
00:42:46,440 --> 00:42:47,817
Your ship came down.

406
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:51,641
Jack managed to pull you
from the wreckage.

407
00:42:53,138 --> 00:42:54,867
But none of your crew survived.

408
00:43:03,000 --> 00:43:04,011
What do you mean?

409
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:06,406
You are the only one that made it.

410
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:11,141
I am sorry.

411
00:43:19,040 --> 00:43:21,349
You have been in delta sleep for a long time.

412
00:43:24,200 --> 00:43:26,248
Some disorientation is normal.

413
00:43:26,800 --> 00:43:27,714
How long?

414
00:43:32,520 --> 00:43:33,620
Sixty years.

415
00:43:34,210 --> 00:43:35,370
At least.

416
00:43:46,800 --> 00:43:48,409
I have to get back to our ship.

417
00:43:55,320 --> 00:43:57,925
It's too dangerous down there.
You need to rest.

418
00:44:08,961 --> 00:44:09,844
Vika...

419
00:44:12,680 --> 00:44:13,743
Don't touch me.

420
00:44:18,120 --> 00:44:20,729
Your ship's re-entry was triggered
by a beacon...

421
00:44:21,424 --> 00:44:22,545
from the surface.

422
00:44:24,200 --> 00:44:25,420
Do you know anything about that?

423
00:44:35,036 --> 00:44:36,437
What was your mission?

424
00:44:38,920 --> 00:44:39,949
It's classified.

425
00:44:40,559 --> 00:44:41,957
Well, we have no record of an Odyssey...

426
00:44:41,982 --> 00:44:44,878
I can't tell you anything until I get
the flight recorder from my ship.

427
00:44:45,320 --> 00:44:46,130
Julia,

428
00:44:46,544 --> 00:44:48,335
a lot has changed in 60 years.

429
00:44:56,280 --> 00:44:57,588
While you were in delta sleep,

430
00:44:59,000 --> 00:45:00,054
Earth was attacked.

431
00:45:01,960 --> 00:45:03,132
Call them scavs.

432
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:07,901
They destroyed our moon
and with that half...

433
00:45:08,033 --> 00:45:08,999
the planet.

434
00:45:11,400 --> 00:45:12,465
Then they invaded.

435
00:45:13,600 --> 00:45:14,715
We won the war,

436
00:45:15,960 --> 00:45:17,153
but Earth was ruined.

437
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:20,039
Everyone is on Titan now.

438
00:45:20,070 --> 00:45:21,589
It's a moon of Saturn or on the...

439
00:45:22,871 --> 00:45:24,742
space station, getting ready to go.

440
00:45:27,440 --> 00:45:29,762
We are here for security
and drone maintenance.

441
00:45:32,800 --> 00:45:34,028
We are the mop-up crew.

442
00:45:56,342 --> 00:45:57,604
You have lost people.

443
00:45:59,800 --> 00:46:00,648
Everything.

444
00:46:04,240 --> 00:46:05,953
If you want to be alone,
we understand.

445
00:46:18,880 --> 00:46:19,932
The drones...

446
00:46:20,338 --> 00:46:21,848
killed her entire crew.

447
00:46:25,480 --> 00:46:26,630
If I had not gotten there...

448
00:46:26,655 --> 00:46:28,180
I want her gone first thing.

449
00:46:28,520 --> 00:46:29,288
Vika?

450
00:46:31,480 --> 00:46:32,694
Do you have any memories...

451
00:46:33,030 --> 00:46:34,210
before the mission?

452
00:46:36,320 --> 00:46:37,608
Before the security wipe?

453
00:46:40,440 --> 00:46:42,075
Our job is not to remember.

454
00:46:44,560 --> 00:46:45,481
Remember?

455
00:46:46,419 --> 00:46:47,715
Do you remember her?

456
00:46:53,400 --> 00:46:54,314
Jack...

457
00:46:55,360 --> 00:46:58,447
That was a scav beacon
that brought her down.

458
00:47:00,600 --> 00:47:02,601
We don't know who she is.

459
00:47:04,930 --> 00:47:06,180
Or what she is.

460
00:47:09,520 --> 00:47:11,036
Let's just get through the night.

461
00:47:12,040 --> 00:47:12,802
Ok?

462
00:47:51,740 --> 00:47:53,005
You fly that thing?

463
00:47:55,243 --> 00:47:56,083
Yes.

464
00:48:00,400 --> 00:48:01,498
What happens now?

465
00:48:04,767 --> 00:48:06,241
The Tet will be online soon.

466
00:48:06,982 --> 00:48:07,831
Victoria,

467
00:48:08,167 --> 00:48:09,459
will report your rescue.

468
00:48:11,040 --> 00:48:12,621
They will send someone down for you.

469
00:48:14,600 --> 00:48:15,644
From the Tet?

470
00:48:16,916 --> 00:48:17,761
Yes.

471
00:48:22,120 --> 00:48:24,173
I need to get the flight recorder
from my ship.

472
00:48:25,866 --> 00:48:27,805
The scavs, they move at night.

473
00:48:29,080 --> 00:48:31,313
They could be all over it by now.
I need to know what happened.

474
00:48:35,120 --> 00:48:36,467
You need to know what happened.

475
00:48:38,760 --> 00:48:39,623
Please.

476
00:49:03,640 --> 00:49:04,350
Jack?

477
00:49:05,186 --> 00:49:05,764
Jack?

478
00:49:05,921 --> 00:49:07,234
What are you doing?

479
00:49:07,323 --> 00:49:08,788
Vika, she is a flight officer.

480
00:49:08,898 --> 00:49:11,515
She wants to see her ship
and secure the flight recorder.

481
00:49:12,360 --> 00:49:13,850
Now, you would want the same thing.

482
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:15,096
<i>Jack I...</i>

483
00:49:17,811 --> 00:49:19,166
can't protect you.

484
00:49:23,000 --> 00:49:24,031
No I understand.

485
00:49:27,480 --> 00:49:28,616
This one is on me.

486
00:50:12,312 --> 00:50:13,421
I could not save them.

487
00:50:25,560 --> 00:50:26,219
Jack.

488
00:50:26,657 --> 00:50:27,467
Jack!

489
00:50:32,120 --> 00:50:33,451
Jack, can you hear me?

490
00:51:06,920 --> 00:51:08,366
Alright, it's time to go.

491
00:51:08,626 --> 00:51:09,501
Jack.

492
00:51:10,960 --> 00:51:11,938
I found it.

493
00:51:24,845 --> 00:51:25,640
Jack!

494
00:52:31,520 --> 00:52:34,205
<i>Tower 49, how are you
all this lovely morning?</i>

495
00:52:34,800 --> 00:52:36,220
Another day in paradise.

496
00:52:38,712 --> 00:52:39,610
Sally...

497
00:52:40,600 --> 00:52:41,313
Jack...

498
00:52:42,188 --> 00:52:44,561
took a pre-dawn patrol

499
00:52:45,360 --> 00:52:46,452
and...

500
00:52:47,909 --> 00:52:49,279
went off-comm

501
00:52:51,200 --> 00:52:53,566
near the canyons in 17.

502
00:52:54,481 --> 00:52:56,847
Now I know,
I know we are low on drones,

503
00:52:57,680 --> 00:52:58,745
but...

504
00:53:00,636 --> 00:53:03,067
requesting one to sweep the area.

505
00:53:06,520 --> 00:53:07,758
Just a quick scout.

506
00:53:08,880 --> 00:53:10,342
<i>Copy 49,</i>

507
00:53:10,366 --> 00:53:13,438
<i>tasking 185 to Grid 22.</i>

508
00:53:47,760 --> 00:53:51,080
And how can a man die better
Than facing fearful odds

509
00:53:51,821 --> 00:53:53,595
For the ashes of his fathers

510
00:53:54,915 --> 00:53:56,835
And the temples of his Gods

511
00:54:14,038 --> 00:54:15,655
I have been watching you, Jack.

512
00:54:17,348 --> 00:54:18,434
You are curious.

513
00:54:19,772 --> 00:54:21,676
What are you looking for in those books?

514
00:54:23,360 --> 00:54:25,215
Do they bring back old memories?

515
00:54:26,320 --> 00:54:27,941
You won't get anything from me.

516
00:54:28,800 --> 00:54:30,213
My memory has been wiped,

517
00:54:30,275 --> 00:54:31,824
to protect the security...
the security of the mission, yes.

518
00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:36,882
You can't have your precious memory

519
00:54:36,907 --> 00:54:39,228
falling into the wrong hands,
now can you?

520
00:54:40,800 --> 00:54:41,601
Tell me.

521
00:54:42,400 --> 00:54:43,518
Have you ever met a...

522
00:54:44,549 --> 00:54:45,478
scav...

523
00:54:45,775 --> 00:54:46,737
up close?

524
00:54:48,560 --> 00:54:49,524
Of course not.

525
00:54:50,133 --> 00:54:51,737
You just repair drones.

526
00:54:53,120 --> 00:54:55,348
Don't go into the radiation zone.

527
00:54:56,320 --> 00:54:58,108
Don't ask too many questions.

528
00:54:59,680 --> 00:55:01,036
Not part of the...

529
00:55:02,358 --> 00:55:03,768
job description.

530
00:55:05,629 --> 00:55:06,551
Lights.

531
00:55:30,360 --> 00:55:31,655
We are not alien, Jack.

532
00:55:32,880 --> 00:55:33,913
We are human.

533
00:55:35,364 --> 00:55:37,496
Of course for us,
being human is a problem.

534
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:44,360
Old stealth fighter tech.

535
00:55:44,754 --> 00:55:46,346
Shields us from your scanners.

536
00:55:47,000 --> 00:55:48,080
Vocal scrambling.

537
00:55:49,400 --> 00:55:50,790
Can you hear me Jack?

538
00:55:51,880 --> 00:55:53,689
Keeps your drones confused.

539
00:55:54,945 --> 00:55:55,715
Well,

540
00:55:56,783 --> 00:55:58,117
most of the time.

541
00:55:59,242 --> 00:56:01,711
The drones are programmed...
To kill humans Jack.

542
00:56:02,080 --> 00:56:04,414
You saw what they did
to those sleep pods.

543
00:56:05,480 --> 00:56:06,935
You almost got yourself,

544
00:56:06,959 --> 00:56:08,942
blown
to bits protecting that woman.

545
00:56:14,200 --> 00:56:15,372
Why did you do that?

546
00:56:16,960 --> 00:56:18,110
Anyone would have.

547
00:56:18,760 --> 00:56:19,776
Anyone.

548
00:56:21,640 --> 00:56:22,641
Interesting.

549
00:56:22,690 --> 00:56:24,088
We are wasting our time.

550
00:56:24,920 --> 00:56:26,276
The drone will track him here.

551
00:56:26,920 --> 00:56:28,080
That's Sergeant Sykes.

552
00:56:28,960 --> 00:56:31,437
He thinks I am a fool
for having brought you here.

553
00:56:38,320 --> 00:56:39,958
I hope you prove him wrong.

554
00:56:51,840 --> 00:56:54,394
Mission, I am picking up a bio trail
somewhere near the west canyons.

555
00:56:54,419 --> 00:56:55,902
Can you confirm the sequence?

556
00:56:56,001 --> 00:56:57,050
<i>Stand by.</i>

557
00:56:59,320 --> 00:57:01,527
<i>DNA confirmed.
It's Jack.</i>

558
00:57:04,280 --> 00:57:05,595
<i>Vika, are you ok?</i>

559
00:57:06,440 --> 00:57:08,447
<i>Everything good between you two?</i>

560
00:57:09,120 --> 00:57:10,048
Of course.

561
00:57:10,640 --> 00:57:12,749
<i>You are still an effective team?</i>

562
00:57:13,194 --> 00:57:14,280
We are great.

563
00:57:16,640 --> 00:57:17,561
Never better.

564
00:57:18,080 --> 00:57:20,084
We were running a ground game,
and losing.

565
00:57:20,560 --> 00:57:22,401
So we decided, what the hell?

566
00:57:22,648 --> 00:57:24,265
We have got to throw the long ball.

567
00:57:25,440 --> 00:57:28,194
It took us decades just
to crack the GPS codes.

568
00:57:29,000 --> 00:57:30,554
That's how you brought down the Odyssey.

569
00:57:33,920 --> 00:57:34,704
Why?

570
00:57:36,480 --> 00:57:38,276
The Odyssey is compact reactor,

571
00:57:38,434 --> 00:57:39,759
courtesy of NASA.

572
00:57:40,200 --> 00:57:41,931
Very hard to come by.

573
00:57:44,240 --> 00:57:45,764
Did you like the show last night?

574
00:57:49,720 --> 00:57:51,811
That was just one fuel cell.

575
00:57:53,280 --> 00:57:55,225
Imagine what 10 of them will do,

576
00:57:56,360 --> 00:57:57,295
with a core...

577
00:57:57,654 --> 00:57:59,365
of weapons-grade plutonium.

578
00:58:00,680 --> 00:58:01,758
We have a nuke,

579
00:58:02,545 --> 00:58:04,104
and we have a drone to carry it.

580
00:58:05,075 --> 00:58:06,763
But we can't access it.

581
00:58:07,482 --> 00:58:09,003
It doesn't know who we are.

582
00:58:11,360 --> 00:58:12,840
But it knows you Jack.

583
00:58:20,520 --> 00:58:22,680
We need you to program the drone.

584
00:58:23,960 --> 00:58:26,281
Have it carry our nuke up to the Tet.

585
00:58:32,560 --> 00:58:33,836
End this war.

586
00:58:38,040 --> 00:58:39,474
There are people up there.

587
00:58:42,120 --> 00:58:43,044
Sergeant.

588
00:58:43,440 --> 00:58:45,707
Program the drone to return to the Tet.

589
00:58:47,720 --> 00:58:49,746
It needs to go right to the center.

590
00:58:52,386 --> 00:58:53,558
Screw you.

591
00:58:56,760 --> 00:58:58,017
We have not got time for this.

592
00:59:23,640 --> 00:59:24,766
Hey. Hey!

593
00:59:36,800 --> 00:59:37,548
No.

594
00:59:44,549 --> 00:59:45,710
Let's go!
Get him up.

595
01:00:42,360 --> 01:00:43,169
Mission,

596
01:00:43,193 --> 01:00:44,840
185 just went off-grid.

597
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:46,968
<i>Copy Tower, we are seeing the same thing.</i>

598
01:00:47,160 --> 01:00:48,899
Permission to task two additional drones?

599
01:00:50,360 --> 01:00:51,678
If one drone is here,

600
01:00:52,500 --> 01:00:53,828
more will come.

601
01:00:54,880 --> 01:00:56,719
And they won't stop until they find me.

602
01:00:57,560 --> 01:00:59,281
They will turn this place to dust.

603
01:01:00,520 --> 01:01:01,562
But if you let us go,

604
01:01:02,163 --> 01:01:03,341
I will call them off.

605
01:01:08,360 --> 01:01:09,505
It's your only chance.

606
01:01:24,680 --> 01:01:26,000
I have been to your...

607
01:01:27,400 --> 01:01:29,000
radiation zones.

608
01:01:30,560 --> 01:01:31,857
If you are looking for the truth,

609
01:01:33,720 --> 01:01:35,138
that's where you will find it.

610
01:01:49,760 --> 01:01:51,529
You have risked all our lives.

611
01:01:51,880 --> 01:01:52,922
Everything.

612
01:01:53,600 --> 01:01:55,477
What makes you think he is different?

613
01:01:57,760 --> 01:01:58,664
She does.

614
01:02:55,154 --> 01:02:56,010
<i>Mission,</i>

615
01:02:56,600 --> 01:02:58,631
<i>I have found my tech over in 37.</i>

616
01:02:59,277 --> 01:03:00,530
<i>You can call off the search.</i>

617
01:03:00,800 --> 01:03:02,100
<i>Copy that Tower.</i>

618
01:03:02,124 --> 01:03:03,326
<i>Glad Jack is safe.</i>

619
01:03:03,480 --> 01:03:06,062
<i>Tasking the other drones back
to rig support.</i>

620
01:03:30,006 --> 01:03:31,385
Where are we going now?

621
01:03:34,172 --> 01:03:35,237
Who are you?

622
01:03:39,000 --> 01:03:40,354
What are not you telling me?

623
01:03:42,240 --> 01:03:43,276
Jack I...

624
01:03:43,692 --> 01:03:45,342
What were you doing on the Odyssey?

625
01:03:46,480 --> 01:03:47,589
What was your mission?

626
01:03:51,453 --> 01:03:53,359
It was a research flight to Titan.

627
01:03:53,890 --> 01:03:54,847
My first.

628
01:03:56,080 --> 01:03:58,000
That's what it was supposed to be.

629
01:04:01,080 --> 01:04:04,992
Six weeks to launch, deep space
scanners picked up an alien object.

630
01:04:05,880 --> 01:04:07,606
We were reassigned to investigate.

631
01:04:09,232 --> 01:04:10,591
They put us all in delta.

632
01:04:10,640 --> 01:04:11,669
They must have...

633
01:04:12,208 --> 01:04:13,998
woken you and Victoria first.

634
01:04:18,871 --> 01:04:19,714
What?

635
01:04:20,440 --> 01:04:21,682
That object...

636
01:04:22,560 --> 01:04:23,893
was the Tet Jack.

637
01:04:25,320 --> 01:04:26,142
The Tet...

638
01:04:26,759 --> 01:04:28,151
was our mission.

639
01:04:31,960 --> 01:04:33,220
That's impossible.

640
01:04:34,920 --> 01:04:36,071
That's impossible!

641
01:04:37,134 --> 01:04:38,837
Who are you?

642
01:04:42,240 --> 01:04:43,392
I am your wife.

643
01:04:48,553 --> 01:04:50,040
I don't know what happened,

644
01:04:51,011 --> 01:04:52,819
but you are not who you think you are.

645
01:05:01,960 --> 01:05:03,176
Jack, we were here.

646
01:05:05,360 --> 01:05:07,058
You asked me to meet you,

647
01:05:07,762 --> 01:05:09,449
brought me up on top of the world.

648
01:05:15,160 --> 01:05:17,188
I could tell you were nervous that day.

649
01:05:18,609 --> 01:05:20,056
It was right here Jack.

650
01:05:25,889 --> 01:05:26,795
You said,

651
01:05:27,800 --> 01:05:28,983
Look through here,

652
01:05:30,874 --> 01:05:32,483
and I will show you the future.

653
01:05:35,160 --> 01:05:36,473
And I held up a ring.

654
01:05:57,547 --> 01:05:58,708
And you said...

655
01:05:58,874 --> 01:05:59,807
Yes.

656
01:06:07,720 --> 01:06:08,823
There you are.

657
01:06:11,719 --> 01:06:12,994
There you are.

658
01:06:38,313 --> 01:06:39,135
Hi.

659
01:06:39,560 --> 01:06:40,674
Hello.

660
01:06:44,069 --> 01:06:45,111
Come on.

661
01:07:48,160 --> 01:07:49,227
<i>Vika, I am coming in.</i>

662
01:07:51,880 --> 01:07:54,261
<i>Do not report to Mission until I get back.
Do you copy?</i>

663
01:07:56,800 --> 01:07:57,792
<i>Do you copy?</i>

664
01:08:15,360 --> 01:08:16,080
Vika,

665
01:08:16,436 --> 01:08:17,420
open the door.

666
01:08:17,840 --> 01:08:19,178
Stay away from me.

667
01:08:21,280 --> 01:08:22,496
I don't want to hear it.

668
01:08:23,242 --> 01:08:24,422
It's not safe here,

669
01:08:25,125 --> 01:08:26,754
and we need to leave, now.

670
01:08:30,520 --> 01:08:31,843
It was always her.

671
01:08:35,360 --> 01:08:36,462
Was not it?

672
01:08:37,800 --> 01:08:38,720
Vika...

673
01:08:44,804 --> 01:08:45,873
She is my wife.

674
01:09:02,240 --> 01:09:04,142
Mission, this is Tower 49.

675
01:09:04,840 --> 01:09:06,205
<i>Go ahead 49.</i>

676
01:09:06,360 --> 01:09:07,173
No.

677
01:09:08,280 --> 01:09:10,252
I am having a problem with my technician.

678
01:09:10,480 --> 01:09:12,158
No, you don't know what you are doing.

679
01:09:12,235 --> 01:09:14,025
He found a survivor at the crash site.

680
01:09:14,129 --> 01:09:15,169
You have got to listen to me.

681
01:09:15,194 --> 01:09:16,655
She is impeding his abilities,

682
01:09:18,358 --> 01:09:20,218
and he is unfit for service.

683
01:09:20,480 --> 01:09:21,811
No, no, no, no.

684
01:09:21,960 --> 01:09:23,710
<i>I am sorry to hear that Vika.</i>

685
01:09:25,160 --> 01:09:27,208
<i>Are you still an effective team?</i>

686
01:09:27,923 --> 01:09:28,801
Vika...

687
01:09:29,314 --> 01:09:30,926
Open the goddamn door, Vika!

688
01:09:31,440 --> 01:09:32,270
No.

689
01:09:36,880 --> 01:09:38,676
We are not an effective team.

690
01:10:01,034 --> 01:10:01,945
Vika please.

691
01:10:02,698 --> 01:10:03,997
We have to go now.

692
01:10:04,115 --> 01:10:05,105
I am not,

693
01:10:05,359 --> 01:10:06,735
I am not going
anywhere with you Jack.

694
01:10:06,760 --> 01:10:07,935
There is a place I know.

695
01:10:08,892 --> 01:10:10,028
We will be safe.

696
01:10:10,846 --> 01:10:12,107
I am going to Titan.

697
01:10:15,120 --> 01:10:16,201
There is no Titan.

698
01:10:16,960 --> 01:10:18,325
They lied to us.

699
01:10:18,520 --> 01:10:20,073
Just stay away from me.

700
01:10:20,960 --> 01:10:21,830
Vika,

701
01:10:22,431 --> 01:10:23,249
please,

702
01:10:23,924 --> 01:10:25,080
there are things...

703
01:10:25,400 --> 01:10:26,502
Things you need to know.

704
01:10:26,527 --> 01:10:28,170
I don't want to know!

705
01:10:33,187 --> 01:10:33,921
Jack...

706
01:11:13,640 --> 01:11:14,770
<i>Hi Jack.</i>

707
01:11:15,343 --> 01:11:17,251
<i>I don't believe
we have had the pleasure.</i>

708
01:11:18,960 --> 01:11:20,235
What have you done?

709
01:11:20,520 --> 01:11:22,725
<i>You can't blame yourself for this.</i>

710
01:11:22,878 --> 01:11:24,415
<i>Drones are unreliable.</i>

711
01:11:24,440 --> 01:11:26,178
<i>Sometimes things go wrong.</i>

712
01:11:27,360 --> 01:11:28,381
Go wrong?

713
01:11:31,787 --> 01:11:33,118
You killed her.

714
01:11:33,400 --> 01:11:34,445
<i>I know,</i>

715
01:11:34,469 --> 01:11:35,529
<i>it's tragic.</i>

716
01:11:35,995 --> 01:11:37,792
<i>She was a wonderful person.</i>

717
01:11:38,331 --> 01:11:39,116
<i>Jack,</i>

718
01:11:39,491 --> 01:11:41,042
<i>we want to bring you in.</i>

719
01:11:42,240 --> 01:11:44,111
<i>I have been authorized to tell you</i>

720
01:11:44,136 --> 01:11:46,244
<i>we are going to assign you
a new mission.</i>

721
01:11:46,960 --> 01:11:48,642
<i>You and the survivor.</i>

722
01:11:55,440 --> 01:11:57,343
<i>There is a lot of interest up here.</i>

723
01:11:57,571 --> 01:11:58,571
<i>Bring her up.</i>

724
01:11:58,800 --> 01:12:01,188
<i>We can debrief,
then anything is possible.</i>

725
01:12:02,760 --> 01:12:04,579
<i>It's time to come home Jack.</i>

726
01:12:06,320 --> 01:12:07,165
<i>Jack?</i>

727
01:12:08,587 --> 01:12:09,524
<i>Jack?</i>

728
01:12:21,080 --> 01:12:21,804
Jack...

729
01:12:24,760 --> 01:12:25,718
I am sorry.

730
01:12:38,626 --> 01:12:39,489
Hang on.

731
01:13:01,200 --> 01:13:02,201
Lightning.

732
01:13:02,760 --> 01:13:03,761
That's the plan.

733
01:13:39,280 --> 01:13:40,520
We need cover.

734
01:13:41,450 --> 01:13:42,239
There.

735
01:15:29,560 --> 01:15:30,446
Are you ok?

736
01:15:30,598 --> 01:15:31,126
No.

737
01:15:42,320 --> 01:15:43,812
Don't worry, we are staying out of there.

738
01:15:53,440 --> 01:15:54,441
Are we gonna die?

739
01:15:54,600 --> 01:15:55,442
No!

740
01:15:59,000 --> 01:15:59,728
Maybe.

741
01:16:01,520 --> 01:16:02,337
Jack!

742
01:16:42,560 --> 01:16:44,081
Son of a bitch.

743
01:16:52,760 --> 01:16:53,761
Wait here.

744
01:17:32,868 --> 01:17:34,060
Who is it?

745
01:18:13,640 --> 01:18:14,301
Hey!

746
01:18:15,467 --> 01:18:16,340
Wait!

747
01:18:17,600 --> 01:18:18,410
Wait!

748
01:18:19,320 --> 01:18:20,066
Hey!

749
01:18:39,301 --> 01:18:40,507
Drop your weapon!

750
01:18:53,590 --> 01:18:54,770
It's...

751
01:18:56,320 --> 01:18:57,196
It's ok.

752
01:19:01,600 --> 01:19:02,587
Don't move!

753
01:19:06,320 --> 01:19:07,689
We have to shut that drone...

754
01:19:08,337 --> 01:19:09,212
down.

755
01:19:11,440 --> 01:19:12,441
Stop moving!

756
01:19:12,640 --> 01:19:13,415
Jack!

757
01:20:20,360 --> 01:20:21,320
It's ok.

758
01:20:42,872 --> 01:20:43,786
Julia.

759
01:20:46,800 --> 01:20:47,677
Julia!

760
01:20:57,736 --> 01:20:58,487
Don't.

761
01:20:59,009 --> 01:21:00,120
Don't touch me.

762
01:21:18,779 --> 01:21:19,739
Hold on.

763
01:21:20,840 --> 01:21:21,677
Just hold on.

764
01:21:53,400 --> 01:21:54,439
Jack Harper,

765
01:21:55,048 --> 01:21:56,368
Tech-52.

766
01:23:06,040 --> 01:23:06,994
Hey.

767
01:23:07,800 --> 01:23:09,041
There you are.

768
01:23:13,520 --> 01:23:14,900
What happened?
Are you ok?

769
01:23:15,520 --> 01:23:17,640
That bogey came across the border
and then I lost you.

770
01:23:21,480 --> 01:23:22,593
False alarm.

771
01:23:27,120 --> 01:23:28,591
I should get back out there.

772
01:23:29,120 --> 01:23:31,208
You come all the way home,
and I don't get a kiss?

773
01:23:43,165 --> 01:23:44,542
What's going on up there?

774
01:23:46,360 --> 01:23:47,463
I was thinking...

775
01:23:49,560 --> 01:23:50,961
Why don't you come down with me?

776
01:23:51,993 --> 01:23:53,140
To the surface?

777
01:23:54,820 --> 01:23:56,179
We could go right now.

778
01:23:57,040 --> 01:23:58,062
Now?

779
01:23:59,440 --> 01:24:00,310
Yeah.

780
01:24:01,360 --> 01:24:02,442
Are you serious?

781
01:24:03,018 --> 01:24:05,169
You won't believe what's down there.

782
01:24:10,200 --> 01:24:11,104
Jack...

783
01:24:12,840 --> 01:24:14,729
You know the regulations.

784
01:24:15,720 --> 01:24:16,432
Yes.

785
01:24:18,720 --> 01:24:21,219
Can we not do this again?
I am done talking about it.

786
01:24:24,840 --> 01:24:25,727
Ok.

787
01:25:15,160 --> 01:25:16,355
This is gonna hurt.

788
01:25:28,120 --> 01:25:29,532
Hell of a day Bob?

789
01:26:55,794 --> 01:26:57,335
You always loved this song.

790
01:27:01,880 --> 01:27:02,859
I am not him.

791
01:27:06,520 --> 01:27:07,538
I know I am not.

792
01:27:11,600 --> 01:27:12,739
But I have loved you...

793
01:27:16,226 --> 01:27:17,887
for as long as I can remember.

794
01:27:19,960 --> 01:27:21,401
I don't know how else to say it.

795
01:27:27,604 --> 01:27:29,410
You know what you said to me once?

796
01:27:32,040 --> 01:27:34,930
You said when it was all over, you
would build me a house on a lake.

797
01:27:38,945 --> 01:27:40,410
We would grow old and...

798
01:27:40,777 --> 01:27:42,187
fat together.

799
01:27:44,075 --> 01:27:45,273
And we would fight.

800
01:27:47,080 --> 01:27:48,247
Maybe drink too much.

801
01:27:50,320 --> 01:27:51,518
Real romantic.

802
01:27:56,520 --> 01:27:58,364
And then we would die...

803
01:28:00,440 --> 01:28:02,492
and be buried in a meadow by the lake.

804
01:28:05,690 --> 01:28:07,883
And the world would forget about us.

805
01:28:12,093 --> 01:28:13,982
But we would always have each other.

806
01:28:17,960 --> 01:28:19,114
I remember.

807
01:28:21,320 --> 01:28:23,206
Those memories are yours, Jack.

808
01:28:25,522 --> 01:28:26,613
They are ours.

809
01:28:29,100 --> 01:28:30,101
They are you.

810
01:29:32,220 --> 01:29:33,254
Good morning.

811
01:29:39,960 --> 01:29:41,760
I wanted to spend
the rest of my life here.

812
01:29:44,320 --> 01:29:45,526
You still can.

813
01:29:49,483 --> 01:29:50,517
I have to go.

814
01:29:51,920 --> 01:29:53,603
Those people need my help.

815
01:30:01,052 --> 01:30:02,867
We will come back when it's over.

816
01:30:05,027 --> 01:30:06,113
Promise me.

817
01:30:08,600 --> 01:30:10,065
We will come back when it's over.

818
01:30:47,520 --> 01:30:49,284
You had me worried for a second.

819
01:30:51,160 --> 01:30:52,722
I thought you were not coming back.

820
01:30:56,200 --> 01:30:57,801
Well, I had to prove him wrong.

821
01:31:01,160 --> 01:31:02,560
You look like shit.

822
01:31:05,360 --> 01:31:06,687
You should see the other guy.

823
01:31:07,200 --> 01:31:09,095
If I had told you
what you would find out there,

824
01:31:09,189 --> 01:31:10,679
you would have thought I was crazy.

825
01:31:12,027 --> 01:31:13,132
I still do.

826
01:31:15,840 --> 01:31:16,903
Malcolm Beech.

827
01:31:16,928 --> 01:31:17,997
Julia Harper.

828
01:31:26,564 --> 01:31:27,524
Come on.

829
01:31:34,360 --> 01:31:36,930
<i>Mission, I am picking up a bio-trail
somewhere near the West Canyons.</i>

830
01:31:37,041 --> 01:31:38,539
<i>Can you confirm the sequence?</i>

831
01:31:38,880 --> 01:31:40,094
<i>Stand by.</i>

832
01:31:41,558 --> 01:31:43,360
<i>DNA confirmed, it's Jack.</i>

833
01:31:44,720 --> 01:31:45,530
<i>Mission,</i>

834
01:31:45,853 --> 01:31:47,548
<i>185 just went off-grid.</i>

835
01:31:48,040 --> 01:31:50,079
<i>Copy, Tower.
We are seeing the same thing.</i>

836
01:32:01,085 --> 01:32:04,280
I had been in the army less than a year
when that unholy Tet arrived.

837
01:32:06,240 --> 01:32:07,804
I saw the moon get taken out.

838
01:32:08,430 --> 01:32:10,017
Right up there in the night sky.

839
01:32:12,600 --> 01:32:13,761
I could not believe it.

840
01:32:15,520 --> 01:32:17,566
After that, nature took over.

841
01:32:19,360 --> 01:32:21,181
There is bedrock around Chicago,

842
01:32:21,278 --> 01:32:24,485
so we were spared the worst
of the waves and the quakes.

843
01:32:27,080 --> 01:32:28,532
Most people just starved.

844
01:32:30,760 --> 01:32:32,803
Then the Tet sent troop ships down.

845
01:32:34,000 --> 01:32:35,264
The doors opened,

846
01:32:36,960 --> 01:32:38,225
and out you came.

847
01:32:40,480 --> 01:32:42,488
Astronaut Jack Harper.

848
01:32:44,485 --> 01:32:45,816
Thousands of you.

849
01:32:48,880 --> 01:32:50,035
Memory wiped.

850
01:32:52,320 --> 01:32:53,541
Programmed to kill.

851
01:32:55,680 --> 01:32:57,541
They had taken one of our best...

852
01:32:59,052 --> 01:33:00,463
and turned him against us.

853
01:33:04,400 --> 01:33:05,358
No soul.

854
01:33:08,200 --> 01:33:09,437
No humanity.

855
01:33:13,640 --> 01:33:14,551
The Tet.

856
01:33:16,520 --> 01:33:18,059
What a brilliant machine.

857
01:33:19,965 --> 01:33:23,293
Feeding off one planet
after another for energy.

858
01:33:25,294 --> 01:33:26,339
Phase Two...

859
01:33:26,744 --> 01:33:27,970
was drones.

860
01:33:28,589 --> 01:33:29,658
Repairmen.

861
01:33:30,964 --> 01:33:33,429
50 years of watching those...

862
01:33:33,453 --> 01:33:36,300
hydro rigs suck our planet dry.

863
01:33:39,240 --> 01:33:40,424
Then one day,

864
01:33:43,120 --> 01:33:44,450
I saw you set down.

865
01:33:46,280 --> 01:33:47,622
Another drone to fix.

866
01:33:49,680 --> 01:33:51,152
But in the rubble that day,

867
01:33:52,107 --> 01:33:53,167
was a book.

868
01:33:54,918 --> 01:33:56,074
You picked it up.

869
01:33:57,120 --> 01:33:58,199
You studied it.

870
01:34:00,840 --> 01:34:01,749
And I...

871
01:34:02,280 --> 01:34:04,011
thought I saw a way.

872
01:34:06,742 --> 01:34:08,769
When you stepped in front of
that drone,

873
01:34:08,988 --> 01:34:09,951
and saved her,

874
01:34:11,080 --> 01:34:11,972
I knew.

875
01:34:13,520 --> 01:34:14,762
You were in there,

876
01:34:14,786 --> 01:34:15,863
somewhere.

877
01:34:17,578 --> 01:34:19,996
I just had to find a way
to bring you back.

878
01:34:44,560 --> 01:34:45,757
Watch... watch off.

879
01:34:46,311 --> 01:34:47,812
Eyes on it.
Steady.

880
01:34:48,320 --> 01:34:49,429
Give it some space.

881
01:34:50,794 --> 01:34:52,257
Come on, you are making it nervous.

882
01:34:56,080 --> 01:34:58,052
That is one pissed-off weapon.

883
01:34:59,400 --> 01:35:00,391
No,

884
01:35:00,594 --> 01:35:01,973
it's just a machine.

885
01:35:05,960 --> 01:35:07,166
<i>I am the weapon.</i>

886
01:35:22,376 --> 01:35:26,770
I would love to be there to see
that thing's face when this goes off.

887
01:35:27,600 --> 01:35:29,372
That would be a one-way trip.

888
01:35:29,920 --> 01:35:30,713
Yeah,

889
01:35:31,965 --> 01:35:33,402
but it would be worth it.

890
01:35:51,880 --> 01:35:53,391
Welcome back Commander.

891
01:36:34,399 --> 01:36:35,810
Open the doors!

892
01:37:02,024 --> 01:37:02,852
Shit!

893
01:37:03,180 --> 01:37:04,134
Spread out!

894
01:37:11,800 --> 01:37:13,529
Head down, keep your head down!

895
01:37:44,920 --> 01:37:45,921
Jack!

896
01:37:46,880 --> 01:37:47,874
Follow me!

897
01:38:46,680 --> 01:38:49,126
Come on, you son of a bitch!

898
01:39:50,851 --> 01:39:51,852
Hey!

899
01:40:52,066 --> 01:40:52,753
Jack.

900
01:40:59,600 --> 01:41:00,574
I am ok.

901
01:41:21,960 --> 01:41:23,025
The drone.

902
01:41:23,840 --> 01:41:24,926
Send the drone.

903
01:41:29,960 --> 01:41:30,754
It's gone.

904
01:41:33,800 --> 01:41:35,384
I thought we had it.

905
01:41:37,120 --> 01:41:38,194
I really did.

906
01:41:40,480 --> 01:41:42,124
I can take the bomb myself.

907
01:41:45,160 --> 01:41:47,445
You know it will swat you like a fly.

908
01:41:48,160 --> 01:41:49,249
Not if I go.

909
01:41:52,560 --> 01:41:53,473
No.

910
01:41:55,200 --> 01:41:56,927
She asked you to bring me up.

911
01:41:59,160 --> 01:42:00,325
So bring me up.

912
01:42:03,720 --> 01:42:04,853
We will go together.

913
01:42:21,560 --> 01:42:23,143
It reminds me of home.

914
01:42:34,200 --> 01:42:34,989
Ready?

915
01:43:13,920 --> 01:43:14,772
Jack.

916
01:43:19,560 --> 01:43:20,605
Dream of us.

917
01:43:36,360 --> 01:43:37,187
Jack...

918
01:44:25,960 --> 01:44:27,082
<i>Flight recorder,</i>

919
01:44:27,106 --> 01:44:29,028
<i>playback for the Odyssey mission.</i>

920
01:44:29,480 --> 01:44:31,604
<i>3 May, 2017.</i>

921
01:44:32,042 --> 01:44:33,120
Ok Bob.

922
01:44:34,640 --> 01:44:35,745
Ready for space?

923
01:44:47,600 --> 01:44:48,979
<i>Good morning Odyssey,</i>

924
01:44:49,003 --> 01:44:51,047
<i>from your friends here at Mission Control.</i>

925
01:44:51,200 --> 01:44:53,280
<i>Good morning Mission.
This is Commander Jack Harper.</i>

926
01:44:53,305 --> 01:44:55,443
<i>Thank you for that fantastic wake-up call.</i>

927
01:44:55,840 --> 01:44:57,255
<i>Pre-rendezvous checks complete.</i>

928
01:44:57,280 --> 01:44:59,918
<i>Electrical guidance
and nav systems, all good.</i>

929
01:45:00,840 --> 01:45:02,367
<i>Range behind object,</i>

930
01:45:02,391 --> 01:45:03,918
<i>250 clicks...</i>

931
01:45:04,200 --> 01:45:07,570
12 below V-bar, closure rate
200 kilometers per hour.

932
01:45:08,160 --> 01:45:10,391
<i>Copy that.
It's good to see you Jack.</i>

933
01:45:11,200 --> 01:45:14,121
<i>After 39 days of sleep,
sounds like you are ready to go.</i>

934
01:45:14,880 --> 01:45:16,207
I am ready to go.

935
01:45:17,000 --> 01:45:18,718
<i>Your next burn will bring you up level</i>

936
01:45:18,743 --> 01:45:21,906
<i>and co-speed at 50 kilometer
range, where you will hold.</i>

937
01:45:22,520 --> 01:45:23,221
Copy.

938
01:45:23,245 --> 01:45:26,238
We will hold 50 clicks from object
for sensor scan and evaluation.

939
01:45:27,400 --> 01:45:28,691
Targets look good.

940
01:45:29,040 --> 01:45:30,729
Initiating burn in three...

941
01:45:30,887 --> 01:45:31,593
Two...

942
01:45:31,847 --> 01:45:32,496
One...

943
01:45:32,542 --> 01:45:33,589
Ignition.

944
01:45:37,560 --> 01:45:38,721
<i>We see a good burn.</i>

945
01:45:38,880 --> 01:45:41,112
<i>Are you reading any output
from the object?</i>

946
01:45:41,600 --> 01:45:42,366
Negative.

947
01:45:42,760 --> 01:45:44,343
Zero heat.
No EMR.

948
01:45:45,345 --> 01:45:46,570
There is no sign of life.

949
01:45:46,880 --> 01:45:48,562
<i>How is the rest of the crew doing?</i>

950
01:45:48,920 --> 01:45:51,241
Co-pilot Victoria Olsen
should be up here shortly.

951
01:45:51,400 --> 01:45:52,417
The rest of the crew...

952
01:45:52,612 --> 01:45:54,051
remains in delta sleep.

953
01:45:55,160 --> 01:45:56,279
<i>Copy that.</i>

954
01:45:56,280 --> 01:45:58,399
<i>You missed a hell of a game last night.</i>

955
01:45:58,760 --> 01:46:01,684
What did I tell you guys?
No spoilers about last night's game.

956
01:46:01,840 --> 01:46:03,727
I am looking forward
to watching it when I get back.

957
01:46:04,400 --> 01:46:06,400
You are not talking about
football already, are you?

958
01:46:06,560 --> 01:46:07,790
<i>Good morning Vika.</i>

959
01:46:07,920 --> 01:46:08,970
<i>Good morning Sally.</i>

960
01:46:09,240 --> 01:46:11,235
<i>How are you doing this lovely morning?</i>

961
01:46:11,333 --> 01:46:12,852
Another day in paradise.

962
01:46:14,400 --> 01:46:15,329
Hey.

963
01:46:20,400 --> 01:46:21,451
One for history.

964
01:46:21,520 --> 01:46:22,381
Yeah.

965
01:46:35,760 --> 01:46:37,003
<i>Tech-49,</i>

966
01:46:37,269 --> 01:46:38,910
<i>I have you on approach.</i>

967
01:46:39,560 --> 01:46:40,582
Hello Sally.

968
01:46:42,440 --> 01:46:43,722
It's a busy morning?

969
01:46:44,760 --> 01:46:47,543
<i>I am picking up a second passenger, Jack.</i>

970
01:46:51,400 --> 01:46:52,853
It's Julia Rusakova,

971
01:46:54,440 --> 01:46:56,478
the female survivor from the crashed module.

972
01:46:57,800 --> 01:46:59,562
<i>State your intention.</i>

973
01:47:00,760 --> 01:47:02,154
Deliver the survivor,

974
01:47:02,584 --> 01:47:03,791
as requested.

975
01:47:04,800 --> 01:47:05,791
We are...

976
01:47:08,480 --> 01:47:09,901
a more effective team.

977
01:47:11,920 --> 01:47:13,299
<i>Proceed to entry.</i>

978
01:47:18,960 --> 01:47:20,213
<i>Mission we have a...</i>

979
01:47:20,237 --> 01:47:21,342
<i>situation.</i>

980
01:47:21,640 --> 01:47:25,413
<i>The last burn was spot-on to give
us a 50-click hold from object,</i>

981
01:47:25,941 --> 01:47:28,103
but radar range still decreasing.

982
01:47:28,480 --> 01:47:30,835
We are accelerating toward the object.

983
01:47:31,455 --> 01:47:33,205
We are going to need
full OMS burn to pull away.

984
01:47:33,230 --> 01:47:34,880
Initiate now.
Entering target.

985
01:47:37,097 --> 01:47:38,658
Gimbals set.
Target is good.

986
01:47:38,683 --> 01:47:39,774
Arm forward engines.

987
01:47:40,233 --> 01:47:41,459
Engines on.
Ready?

988
01:47:41,682 --> 01:47:42,596
Let's go.

989
01:47:52,360 --> 01:47:54,793
Mission, we are in full OMS burn,
trying to back out.

990
01:47:55,520 --> 01:47:57,051
There is a lot of vibration.

991
01:47:58,320 --> 01:47:59,684
We are not getting away from this thing.

992
01:47:59,756 --> 01:48:00,670
<i>Odyssey,</i>

993
01:48:00,764 --> 01:48:02,753
<i>telemetry shows
structural overstress.</i>

994
01:48:02,778 --> 01:48:04,888
<i>Knock off the burn.
Do you copy?</i>

995
01:48:05,320 --> 01:48:06,294
Cutting off burn.

996
01:48:08,840 --> 01:48:09,785
Mission.

997
01:48:11,200 --> 01:48:12,386
Mission?
Mission?

998
01:48:12,840 --> 01:48:13,777
Sally?

999
01:48:15,160 --> 01:48:16,855
Increased acceleration toward the object.

1000
01:48:17,200 --> 01:48:19,282
Estimated contact within two minutes.

1001
01:48:24,840 --> 01:48:26,710
I am going to eject the sleep module.

1002
01:48:27,520 --> 01:48:29,685
It's programmed for reinsertion
into Earth orbit.

1003
01:48:29,710 --> 01:48:31,896
I will fly the Command module out
if I break free.

1004
01:48:32,656 --> 01:48:34,685
I want you back there now.
Absolutely not.

1005
01:48:34,750 --> 01:48:35,831
That's an order!
Jack?

1006
01:48:35,856 --> 01:48:36,864
No, we are a team.

1007
01:48:59,720 --> 01:49:02,075
We have got to go, Jack! 30 seconds!

1008
01:49:05,160 --> 01:49:06,294
Dream of us.

1009
01:49:48,360 --> 01:49:49,222
Jack...

1010
01:50:05,600 --> 01:50:08,212
<i>Tech-49, enter at headway speed.</i>

1011
01:50:09,920 --> 01:50:11,219
Entering at headway.

1012
01:50:28,440 --> 01:50:29,646
You buck up, Bob.

1013
01:50:31,000 --> 01:50:32,807
Don't go all shaky on me.

1014
01:51:07,497 --> 01:51:09,364
<i>Jack, I can't help notice</i>

1015
01:51:09,389 --> 01:51:12,297
<i>your respiration
and heart rate have increased.</i>

1016
01:51:13,840 --> 01:51:16,024
I am just excited to finally meet you Sally.

1017
01:51:16,520 --> 01:51:20,933
<i>There is been a pattern of
insubordinate behavior recently.</i>

1018
01:51:22,800 --> 01:51:23,527
Yeah.

1019
01:51:24,600 --> 01:51:26,019
I feel bad about that.

1020
01:51:27,720 --> 01:51:31,520
<i>Voice analysis indicates
you are lying to me Jack.</i>

1021
01:51:31,680 --> 01:51:33,289
<i>Tell me why you are here.</i>

1022
01:51:33,491 --> 01:51:35,383
<i>You have five seconds.</i>

1023
01:51:42,480 --> 01:51:43,998
I want Julia to live.

1024
01:51:46,000 --> 01:51:47,985
I want our species to survive.

1025
01:51:50,790 --> 01:51:52,092
This is the only way.

1026
01:51:58,360 --> 01:52:01,223
<i>Proceed to landing.
Atmosphere provided.</i>

1027
01:53:00,360 --> 01:53:02,575
<i>Welcome home Jack.</i>

1028
01:53:16,394 --> 01:53:17,395
Come on.

1029
01:53:17,680 --> 01:53:20,010
<i>Jack, you are doing the right thing.</i>

1030
01:53:20,920 --> 01:53:22,617
I don't know what you are,

1031
01:53:23,244 --> 01:53:24,648
or where you are from but...

1032
01:53:26,317 --> 01:53:28,687
I would like to tell you about something I read.

1033
01:53:30,240 --> 01:53:31,167
A story...

1034
01:53:32,157 --> 01:53:33,335
from Rome,

1035
01:53:34,360 --> 01:53:35,825
a city you destroyed.

1036
01:53:37,680 --> 01:53:38,817
It's a classic.

1037
01:53:40,240 --> 01:53:41,344
There was a guy,

1038
01:53:42,083 --> 01:53:43,153
Horatius,

1039
01:53:44,240 --> 01:53:46,536
held the bridge alone against a whole army.

1040
01:53:47,582 --> 01:53:49,310
And what Horatius said was,

1041
01:53:50,277 --> 01:53:52,325
How can a man die better...

1042
01:53:52,360 --> 01:53:54,649
<i>You don't have to die Jack.</i>

1043
01:53:54,789 --> 01:53:57,084
<i>She doesn't have to die.</i>

1044
01:53:57,120 --> 01:53:58,418
Everybody dies Sally.

1045
01:53:59,523 --> 01:54:00,926
The thing is, to die well.

1046
01:54:10,400 --> 01:54:11,416
<i>Jack,</i>

1047
01:54:11,440 --> 01:54:14,283
<i>that's not the survivor you promised me.</i>

1048
01:54:15,640 --> 01:54:17,233
No, it's not.

1049
01:54:40,160 --> 01:54:40,862
What...

1050
01:54:41,924 --> 01:54:43,455
Horatius said was,

1051
01:54:43,891 --> 01:54:44,699
How...

1052
01:54:45,363 --> 01:54:46,898
can a man die better.

1053
01:54:49,040 --> 01:54:50,890
Than facing fearful odds,

1054
01:54:52,960 --> 01:54:53,833
Drones!

1055
01:54:54,007 --> 01:54:55,632
Get inside! Get inside!

1056
01:54:56,549 --> 01:54:58,233
For the ashes of his fathers

1057
01:55:01,153 --> 01:55:03,122
And the temples of his Gods

1058
01:55:05,257 --> 01:55:07,247
<i>I created you Jack.</i>

1059
01:55:07,600 --> 01:55:09,682
<i>I am your God.</i>

1060
01:55:22,080 --> 01:55:23,413
Fuck you Sally.

1061
01:56:16,520 --> 01:56:17,250
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Earth,</i></font>

1062
01:56:18,005 --> 01:56:19,146
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>after the war.</i></font>

1063
01:56:21,260 --> 01:56:23,838
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Three years have passed
since I saw your face.</i></font>

1064
01:56:25,880 --> 01:56:27,218
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I wonder if I come to you,</i></font>

1065
01:56:27,359 --> 01:56:28,177
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>at night,</i></font>

1066
01:56:28,318 --> 01:56:29,213
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>in dreams.</i></font>

1067
01:56:30,440 --> 01:56:31,347
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>In the day,</i></font>

1068
01:56:32,362 --> 01:56:33,396
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>as memories.</i></font>

1069
01:56:35,200 --> 01:56:36,519
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Do I haunt your hours,</i></font>

1070
01:56:37,363 --> 01:56:38,803
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>the way you haunted mine?</i></font>

1071
01:56:41,480 --> 01:56:43,105
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>And I wonder if you see me,</i></font>

1072
01:56:43,490 --> 01:56:44,683
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>when you look at her.</i></font>

1073
01:56:57,259 --> 01:56:58,594
Mommy look.

1074
01:57:04,934 --> 01:57:06,257
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>If we have souls,</i></font>

1075
01:57:07,078 --> 01:57:08,765
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>they are made of the love we share.</i></font>

1076
01:57:12,640 --> 01:57:14,124
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Undimmed by time.</i></font>

1077
01:57:16,080 --> 01:57:17,352
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Unbound by death.</i></font>

1078
01:57:36,080 --> 01:57:37,288
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>For three years,</i></font>

1079
01:57:37,460 --> 01:57:39,595
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I searched for the house he built.</i></font>

1080
01:57:41,520 --> 01:57:43,033
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I knew it had to be out there.</i></font>

1081
01:57:46,760 --> 01:57:47,936
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>Because I know him.</i></font>

1082
01:57:56,920 --> 01:57:57,933
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I am him.</i></font>

1083
01:58:01,160 --> 01:58:02,152
Who is that?

1084
01:58:10,538 --> 01:58:11,923
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>I am Jack Harper.</i></font>

1085
01:58:14,332 --> 01:58:15,696
<font color="#f4ff7a"><i>And I am home.</i></font>

1086
01:58:19,077 --> 01:58:22,144
By <font color="#ff80ff">L</font><font color="#ff6aff">E</font><font color="#ff5bff">S</font><font color="#ff3cff">A</font><font color="#ff15ff">I</font><font color="#f200f2">G</font><font color="#e100e1">N</font><font color="#cc00cc">E</font><font color="#bb00bb">U</font><font color="#ae00ae">R</font>
